1. Mailflare, as modified by Seongwoo Hong
   The Mailflare Gorani draws on is not the product Cloudflare publishes: it
   is Seongwoo Hong's own, heavily modified version, reworked for his work
   suites. Only his tweaked parts are here — portions of the file-management
   design, the vault encryption formats (byte layouts), the desktop-sync
   protocol ideas and several document / archive parsers, ported or adapted
   into Gorani. Wherever this repository says "Mailflare", it means that
   modified version.

   His version began as a fork of Mailflare by Cloudflare, Inc.
   (https://github.com/cloudflare/mailflare), under the Apache License. As
   that license requires, Cloudflare's copyright notice stays with whatever
   of its original code those parts still carry: each derived file says so
   in its header, beside the Gorani copyright.

2. mp4-hls-core, from Seongwoo Hong's stream-worker project
   His own code, not a third party's: the ISO-BMFF parser, the keyframe
   index builder and the fMP4 segment assembly, vendored under crates/media/
   as gorani-media (commit 39p) and built to WebAssembly by
   crates/media-wasm for the in-page video player (docs/VIDEO.md). The
   server-side parts of stream-worker (request handling, DASH output, its
   DRM test material) stayed behind. The S3 transport in worker/src/s3.rs
   follows the adapter he wrote for the same project.

3. Vendored file (served as-is, not built): web/public/vendor/argon2.umd.min.js
   is hash-wasm 4.12.0's dist/argon2.umd.min.js (MIT, (c) Dani Biro),
   byte for byte:
     sha256 dcec617a2e1b700fa132d1583a186cb70611113395e869f2dd6cc82b415d3094
